<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="6d9af076">&lt;p&gt;
    Consider how any new learning developed aligns with the overall direction of the organizational learning strategy, how
    it may inform the employee experience and where it sits within the overall employee development pathway.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    A tiered system is recommended, where the learning path advances from a general understanding to more specific and
    job-specific learning. The aim of this approach is to guarantee relevance and customize the learning experiences to
    meet the distinct requirements of each person.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="439d6293"></attribute>
<attribute name="usageGuidance" nodeId="ae2641d9"></attribute>
<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="aa165344">&lt;p&gt;
    This work product outlines the averarching strategy based on the target audience&apos;s requirements. It includes the what,
    how, who, when and where the learning will be delivered. The approach covers learning design, development, delivery,
    assessment, evaluation as well as understanding the technology and infrastructure needs of the program.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
